report.body:
Summary: In curl 8.14.1 the function `Curl_http2_stream_reset_internal()` in lib/http2.c frees the stream context and later reads it again when the server sends RST_STREAM. See lib/http2.c:3987.

```c
static void Curl_http2_stream_reset_internal(struct h2_stream_ctx *sctx)
{
  free(sctx->recvbuf_secure_ptr);
  sctx->reset_pending_flag = TRUE;
  h2_stream_finalize_secure(sctx);
}
```

Impact: remote code execution against any client using HTTP/2.

